\cf2 Introduction\par
Hi. This introduction is for those who haven't played that many text adventures before. This game is set purposefully on Earth, not in space, or on Mars, or under the sea or something stupid like that. The game is set in England in the small (and completely fictional village) of Piddlington. This game is unlike others in that it is possible to have a proper conversation with the characters. To do this you can use the 'converse with' command (the 'talk to' command will not work) and this will usually let you conduct a conversation with the said character. These conversations will usually give you a few hints although you can probably only do this once. The characters can also be asked about things although their responses to this action are pretty limited. This game is not completely realistic or serious but very cynical. Try things that sound completely ridiculous. Most objects have uses although some are just used for show. I also have to say that it is (probably) impossible to achieve the total score although it would be interesting to see what the highest percentage is. Finally if you can't work out how to complete the game there is a built in walkthrough in the game although you will have to discover this for yourself.\par
If you have any questions, comments, ideas, suggestions, conspiracy theories etc. please send them to me at kevkov@hotmail.com. Thankyou.\par
\par
Story\par
The story so far...\par
The last few weeks have been hell. It started off with your sacking as a pizza delivery boy. It continued when you couldn't pay your rent to Mr Malloney, your landlord and local hard-man. You have been having nightmares and Malloney has threatened to send men round to 'sort you out.' You dream of getting away from it all, escaping. One night you are having an even more vivid nightmare. You are running away, being pursued by Malloney's henchmen, suddenly you trip and fall into a giant puddle, it's sucking you in, you try to shout but to no avail, you're sinking further and further...\par
You wake up face down in a puddle on the high street. You've been sleep-walking, again. You remember the times when, as a child, you used to get into all sorts of trouble doing it. You look around, you are lying in the gutter, arse-naked. Bugger. You swear a few oaths and get to your feet. A feeling swells up inside you, you need to get out of this place, you need to escape. In that moment you decide that today is the day that you are going to leave. There, you've said it, but first of course you could do with some clothes...\par
