You are in the middle of a long street. A car sits unobtrusively on one side of the road. Birds circle overhead and grey clouds roll slowly across the sky.  From here, the sky's the limit. You can go north up the street, you could also choose to go south which would lead you down the street or you can go east to the now dead Mrs Walters'  house. \par
\cf1 \par
break into car\par
\cf2 You smash the window of the car and slide through into the drivers seat. The sound of the crash, however, was louder than you had hoped for and alerts several people in the street outside. You may not have much time to make good your escape.  A distant siren sounds...\par
\cf1 \par
drive\par
\cf2 You turn the key and start the car. You speed off, a sense of speed and exhilaration feels your entire body. You feel free. Then, suddenly, a police car swerves into view behind you. Your hope shatters, you've watched countless 'police, camera action!' shows (you sad bastard) and you know how these things generally turn out. You must think fast in order to avoid capture. There is a long winding road with two turnings, you have the choice of either turning left or right.  From behind you hear the sirens of the advancing police cars.  The police cars are getting much closer...\par
\cf1 \par
turn left\par
\cf2 You turn left onto a small, winding road. You look ahead and your heart sinks. Ahead is a large group of sheep, there is no way through. You brake sharply. The police car however is some way behind. You realise that there might be a way out of here. However time is ticking...  The sirens that have dogged you over the last few miles are still audible in the distance.\par
\cf1 \par
turn on radio\par
\cf2 You switch the radio onto Radio Piddlington. 'Accelerator' by Primal Scream bursts out at you which seems quite appropriate given the circumstances. You feel the blood rising in your veins along with the tempo of the song, you're in real car chase mood.\par
\cf1 \par
listen to radio\par
\cf2 "Come on! Come on! Hit the Accelerator! Hit the Accelerator! Come on! Come on! Hit the Accelerator! Hit the Accelerator!"  The sirens seem to get closer...\par
\cf1 \par
exit car\par
\cf2 You jump out of the car quickly and into the lane. Your heart is beating fast as you know that there isn't much time.\par
\cf1 \par
w\par
\cf2 You move west.\par
This bit of country road is much like any other, surrounded by fields and badly signposted. But right now you've probably got more important things on your mind.  From here you can either move north, south or east.  A flock of sheep is here. They appear to be taking as much time as possible to cross the road.  A shephard is here, he is nonchalantly chewing a piece of grass as he coaxes his sheep across.  You can't see the police car, but you can definitely hear it, and it's getting closer...\par
\cf1 \par
shoot shephard\par
\cf2 You level the stun-gun at the innocent shephard and fire. He slumps to the floor unconscious. The sheep instictively begin going off in all directions, a few choosing to gnaw at the slumbering shephard's face.\par
\cf1 \par
n\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
This is the side of the road, A large brown fence with remarkably useful handholds dominates the nearby surroundings.  The options for movement here are to move south and east.  You can't see the police car, but you can definitely hear it, and it's getting closer...\par
\cf1 \par
climb fence\par
\cf2 Due to your pathetic upper body strength you struggle up the fence and fall onto the field at the other side. You land badly, spraining your ankle, and realise with horror that you can barely stand let alone run. For you the chase is over, but maybe you could still get away with it...  The sirens are getting louder and louder...\par
